;; clj-kondo configuration for Jonquil.
;;
;; Adapted from a-private-sibling's `.clj-kondo/config.edn`. That project imports
;; an ObjC binding library's own exported config (its `objc`/`defclass`/`with-block` macros,
;; plus :unquote-not-syntax-quoted for objc's `~x` argument syntax). None of
;; that applies here: Jonquil binds GTK4 through jolt.ffi directly, with no
;; an ObjC binding library dependency and no `~x`-outside-syntax-quote usage anywhere in
;; src/dev (checked by grep; the only `~` in the tree is prose in docstrings
;; and comments, e.g. "~80 bytes", "~200k-char").
;;
;; jolt.ffi itself is not a gitlib dependency with its own clj-kondo config
;; to import: it is a namespace built into the jolt runtime. Measured
;; (2026-09-26, jolt v0.8.12-30-gc9808c39, this project's deps.edn has no
;; :deps at all, just :paths):
;;
;;   clj-kondo --lint "$(jolt path)" --dependencies --copy-configs
;;   => "No configs copied."
;;
;; `jolt path` printed `./src`, this project's own source root, confirming
;; there is no separate dependency tree to export from. So everything below
;; is authored here, not imported.
;;
;; The standard for adding anything here: every entry covers something a
;; MACRO (or, for :output, an intentionally-invalid fixture file) hides from
;; static analysis. None silences a finding about code that could be wrong.
;; If the linter is right and the code is wrong, fix the code.
{:hooks {:analyze-call {jolt.ffi/defcfn hooks.jolt-ffi/defcfn}}

 ;; 1. jolt.ffi/defcfn defines a var per bound C symbol. hooks/jolt_ffi.clj
 ;;    rewrites each call into an equivalent `defn` — see that file for what
 ;;    it fixes and the measured before/after counts.
 ;;
 ;; 2. jolt.ffi/with-c-string-array binds [labels 4] in
 ;;    jonquil.gtk.window/confirm-close! (the alert-dialog button-label
 ;;    array) — a NAME and a SIZE, not let pairs, so `labels` reads as
 ;;    unresolved without this exclude. Measured: this is the only
 ;;    with-c-string-array call site in the project (one occurrence).
 :linters {:unresolved-symbol {:exclude [(jolt.ffi/with-c-string-array)]}}

 ;; dev/smoke/fixtures/*.clj are deliberately invalid or minimal Clojure —
 ;; binary_smoke.clj feeds them to the built jonquil binary to exercise
 ;; unclosed-paren recovery, find, completion, etc. (see that file's own
 ;; comment: "the checked-in dev/smoke/fixtures/*.clj files, never the
 ;; fixtures ... owns"). Linting them as project code is a category error:
 ;; measured, they contribute 10 parse/unresolved-symbol errors (unclosed.clj,
 ;; completion_single.clj, completion_multi.clj, find.clj) that have nothing
 ;; to do with Jonquil's own code and would make `lint:strict` and the
 ;; pre-commit hook permanently red.
 :output {:exclude-files ["dev/smoke/fixtures/"]}}
